Write the Matroska Title element for WebM too.

Connecting to a stream in VLC shows the channel name for the Matroska and MP4
profiles, but for the WebM ones -- VP8 and VP9, software or VAAPI -- it shows
the request URL instead: the channel UUID followed by the profile name.

muxer_mkv.c builds Segment Information with two elements guarded the same way:

    if(!mk->webm)
      ebml_append_bin(q, 0x73a4, mk->uuid, sizeof(mk->uuid));   // SegmentUUID

    if(!mk->webm)
      ebml_append_string(q, 0x7ba9, mk->title);                 // Title

The first guard is right: WebM has no use for SegmentUUID, which exists for
segment linking that WebM does not support. The second is not -- Title is part
of WebM's Segment Information, and libavformat writes it for both. From
matroskaenc.c:

    put_ebml_uint(pb, MATROSKA_ID_TIMECODESCALE, 1000000);
    if ((tag = av_dict_get(s->metadata, "title", NULL, 0)))
        put_ebml_string(pb, MATROSKA_ID_TITLE, tag->value);     <- unconditional
    ...
        if (!IS_WEBM(mkv))
            put_ebml_binary(pb, MATROSKA_ID_SEGMENTUID, ...);   <- guarded

So the title is simply dropped for WebM, the file carries no name, and the
player falls back to whatever it asked for. Emit it in both cases.

Only the two profiles that use the native Matroska muxer with MC_WEBM are
affected. `pass` and HTSP are unrelated: they carry no Matroska container at
all, so there is no Title element to write and their display name comes from
elsewhere.

Confirmed with VLC on the reporting hardware: the WebM profiles now show the
channel name like the Matroska and MP4 ones, instead of the request URL.

The libavformat precedent holds across every ffmpeg spksrc builds against --
4.4.6, 5.1.7, 6.1.3, 7.1.2 and 8.1.2 all emit the title unconditionally and
guard only SEGMENTUID. Not that it governs this patch: the native Matroska
muxer writes its own EBML and never goes through libavformat, so no ffmpeg
version enters into it.

--- src/muxer/muxer_mkv.c.orig
+++ src/muxer/muxer_mkv.c
@@ -232,8 +232,13 @@ mk_build_segment_info(mk_muxer_t *mk)
   if(!mk->webm)
     ebml_append_bin(q, 0x73a4, mk->uuid, sizeof(mk->uuid));   //0x73a4 = SegmentUUID
 
-  if(!mk->webm)
-    ebml_append_string(q, 0x7ba9, mk->title);                 //0x7ba9 = Title
+  /* Title is part of WebM's Segment Information, unlike SegmentUUID above --
+     libavformat writes it for both (matroskaenc.c: the title tag is emitted
+     unconditionally, only SEGMENTUID is guarded by IS_WEBM). Skipping it left
+     players with nothing to show for a webm stream, so VLC fell back to the
+     request URL and displayed the channel UUID and profile name instead of the
+     channel. */
+  ebml_append_string(q, 0x7ba9, mk->title);                   //0x7ba9 = Title
 
   ebml_append_string(q, 0x4d80, "Tvheadend Matroska muxer");  //0x4d80 = MuxingApp
   ebml_append_string(q, 0x5741, app);                         //0x5741 = WritingApp
